What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my @a = (1, 2, 3);
my $r = \@a;
$r->[1] = 20;
my @b = @a;
$b[2] = 30;
say "@a";
```

What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my $d = { k => [ 'x', { y => 'z' } ] };
say $d->{k}[1]{y}, ref $d->{k}, ref $d->{k}[1];
```

What number does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
sub make {
    my $n = shift;
    return sub { return $n++ };
}
my $f = make(5);
my $g = make(5);
$f->() for 1 .. 3;
say $f->() + $g->();
```

